// editor_evaluation.proto — WHAT EVALUATING ELISP IN THE RUNNING EDITOR
// ANSWERED. Shared by the agent's call (EvaluateInEditor), the daemon's push
// to the editor (agentrepl.v1.WatchHostWorkspaceResponse.evaluate), and the editor's answer
// (AnswerEditorEvaluation), so the answer the agent reads is exactly the one
// the editor gave.
//
// ERRORS ARE CAUGHT IN THE EDITOR'S ONE HANDLER: the text is read and
// evaluated inside a single `condition-case` there, never wrapped by the
// caller, so no request bypasses it and text that does not even read is
// answered as a read error rather than breaking the wrapper.

